          "id": "thm-countable-mode-car-has-universal-inductive-limit-norm",
          "concern": "The Statement describes a “unital $*$-homomorphism” into B(H), while the cited definition makes B(H) all bounded operators and the Remarks explicitly avoid asserting that all of them have adjoints without choice. Step 2.1 correctly constructs adjoints for the represented image. Clarify that star-preservation refers to these image adjoints, or name the adjointable-operator subalgebra as target.",
